# Dependency Injection & Navigation

Source of truth: `iOSApp/AGENT.md` §5, §8.

## AppContainer

- Single composition root in `Core/DI/AppContainer.swift`
- Nothing constructs infrastructure with `SomeClass()` outside the container
- Expose `make*UseCase()` and `make*ViewModel(...)` factories
- ViewModels are always created fresh per screen

```swift
func makeChatViewModel(sessionId: String, router: AppRouter) -> ChatViewModel {
    ChatViewModel(
        sessionId: sessionId,
        saveMemoryUseCase: makeSaveMemoryUseCase(),
        router: router
    )
}
```

Prefer creating ViewModels in `navigationDestination` (or equivalent) via the container, then pass into the View.

## AppRouter

- `NavigationStack` + typed `NavigationPath` (iOS 16+) — never `NavigationView`
- `AppRouter` is the only navigation source of truth
- ViewModels call `router.navigate(to:)`, `navigateBack()`, `present(_:)`, `dismissSheet()`
- Deep links go through `AppRouter`
- Inject router with `@EnvironmentObject` — do not prop-drill more than two levels

## Tabs

Root uses `TabView` with Chats / Memories / Settings; tint with `Color.theme.accent`.
